# Database — Migrations (Safe Workflow)

Created: 2026-02-02 05:37 UTC  
Last reviewed: 2026-02-02 05:37 UTC

Schema migrations are high-risk and should be treated as gated actions.

## Principles
- Prefer additive changes (new columns/tables) over destructive changes.
- Backfill in batches for large tables.
- Separate deploy steps: “add column” → “write new path” → “read new path” → “cleanup old”.

## Typical Migration Checklist
- Name is descriptive and reversible where possible.
- Includes an index strategy if adding new query paths.
- Includes a backfill plan (batch size, expected runtime).
- Includes rollback notes.

## “Never Do This Blind”
- `DROP COLUMN`, `DROP TABLE`, `TRUNCATE`
- unbounded backfills on production
- long-running locks on hot tables

